Krita Nova 35 - the color range slider of the HSV Adjustment (Photoshop style)

Below the sliders of Filter > Adjust > HSV/HSL Adjustment, like Photoshop's
Hue/Saturation:

- two hue spectrum bars: the colors as they are (top) and as the adjustment
  turns them (bottom);
- for a color range (Reds ... Magentas, patch 34), its limits between the
  bars: full effect between the two inner bars (dark), fading out towards the
  two outer triangles (light). Drag a limit to move it (they keep their order,
  and the range stays under 360 degrees); drag the range itself to move all
  four. The limits are shown above the bars as "315°/345° \ 15°/45°".
- The bars are centered on the range being edited (red for Master, which has
  no limits). With Colorize or YUV (no color ranges) the slider is hidden.
  Reset puts the limits back to Photoshop's defaults.

KisHueRangeSlider (kis_hsv_adjustment_filter.h/.cpp) is the widget. The limits
are saved per range as "ra_1".."rd_6" (continuous degrees a <= b <= c <= d,
default center -45, -15, +15, +45) and handed to the transformation as
"rangeBounds" (24 values); KisHSVAdjustment::rangeWeight() uses them instead
of the fixed widths of patch 34.
